      headline: "Worked example: \u00a35,589 net R&D credit on glaze formulation automation",
      body: "Take a small pottery in Burslem investing in an automated glaze mixing line and unsure whether process development of that kind qualifies as R&D. Trialling new formulations to hit a consistent finish is usually where the technical uncertainty lives, so the qualifying costs tend to be materials consumed in testing, subcontracted laboratory work and the staff time spent on the trials. Where the development spans two accounting periods, the claim is made for each period separately. Suppose the two periods together support \u00a334,500 of qualifying expenditure, giving a credit of \u00a36,900 at the 20% merged scheme rate. Profits here sit under the \u00a350,000 small profits limit, so the credit is taxed at 19% rather than 25% and \u00a35,589 of it is kept, enough to fund the rest of the installation.",
