    whyHere: "Milton Keynes businesses operate in a fast paced, growth oriented environment. We work with limited company directors and small business owners across Central Milton Keynes, Bletchley, and Wolverton, where logistics, tech, and automotive sectors dominate. Our experienced team combines remote first efficiency with in person meetings at your office or a local workspace. Whether you run a distribution firm near the MK9 grid or a tech startup in MK14, we bring practical tax and compliance support that matches the local pace.",
    businessScene: "Milton Keynes has one of the highest business start up rates outside London, thanks to its strategic location on the M1 and the West Coast Main Line. The city is a national centre for logistics and distribution, with major warehousing and fulfilment operations serving retailers like Argos. The tech and ecommerce sector is concentrated around Central Milton Keynes and the MK1 business parks, while financial services is anchored by Santander UK and Volkswagen Financial Services. Red Bull Racing, based in nearby Brackley, draws on the city for specialist engineering and support roles. The local economy is distinctive for its mix of large corporate HQs and a dense network of small and medium sized suppliers, contractors, and professional service firms.",
