    sectorEmphasis: "Northampton\u2019s sector mix shapes the services we emphasise. A logistics firm based in Brackmills might prioritise VAT compliance on cross-border shipments and capital allowances on warehouse fit-outs. An engineering company in St James often comes to us for R&D claim preparation on process automation projects, where the technical narrative must be precise to withstand HMRC scrutiny. We also work with financial services businesses in the Town Centre, where corporation tax planning and share scheme administration are regular needs. The heritage footwear sector, including suppliers to Church\u2019s Shoes, requires careful stock valuation and margin analysis for partnership tax returns. Healthcare providers, from dental practices to private clinics, need payroll and pension auto-enrolment that handles irregular shift patterns. Across all sectors, we help directors structure dividends efficiently and prepare for exit, whether that means a trade sale to a larger group or a management buyout. Our experience gives local business owners confidence that the advice is technically sound and commercially realistic.",
    keyEmployers: ["Carlsberg UK", "Travis Perkins HQ", "Nationwide Building Society", "Avon Cosmetics UK", "Church's Shoes"],
    localCaseStudy: {
      business_type: "15-employee engineering firm",
      headline: "Worked example: \u00a337,000 R&D expenditure credit on an automated welding line",
      body: "Take a precision engineering company in St James that has put \u00a3185,000 into developing an automated welding line for automotive components and never prepared a claim. The documentation that matters is the record of technical uncertainties, the iterative testing and the specific advance achieved in weld consistency, tied to staff time, materials and subcontractor costs. On those facts the merged scheme expenditure credit at 20 per cent of that \u00a3185,000 is \u00a337,000 before the corporation tax charge on the credit itself, which is usually recycled into the next automation project. A factory roof replacement carried out in the same period is worth looking at separately, since the structures and buildings allowance and the integral features inside the works carry relief that is easily left unclaimed.",
    },
    localFaqs: [
      { question: "Do you have an office in Northampton?", answer: "We operate on a remote-first basis but meet Northampton clients in the Town Centre or at their premises in Brackmills, Abington or St James. We also serve Wellingborough, Kettering, Daventry and Towcester with the same approach." },
      { question: "My logistics company in Brackmills ships to EU customers. Can you handle the VAT?", answer: "Yes. We regularly advise distribution businesses on post-Brexit VAT, including distance selling thresholds, customs entries and postponed accounting. We can also review your margin schemes if you handle second-hand goods." },
      { question: "How do you price for a limited company director with a side business?", answer: "On the number of separate tax positions rather than the number of hours. One director with a single company is one set of accounts, one corporation tax return and one personal return. Add a sole trade alongside it and your own return carries a second set of accounts on the tax-year basis. Add a partnership and there is a partnership return too, with each partner taxed on their profit share. We scope which applies before agreeing anything." },
      { question: "I am a contractor considering IR35 changes. Can you help with a review?", answer: "Yes. We assess your contracts and working practices against HMRC's employment status tests, and we can prepare a status determination statement where your end client requires one. Since April 2021 a medium or large client makes the determination and issues the statement; where the client is small, the determination stays with your own company. That distinction, not the sector, decides how a Northampton engineering or IT contractor should be paid." },
    ],
    nearbyAreas: ["Wellingborough", "Kettering", "Daventry", "Towcester"],
    adjacentTown: { slug: "leicester", name: "Leicester" },
