    businessScene: "Oxford\u2019s economy is defined by its dual character: a globally renowned university and research ecosystem alongside a substantial industrial base. The University of Oxford and its associated colleges, hospitals, and spin-outs dominate the knowledge economy, with the John Radcliffe Hospital and Oxford BioMedica anchoring a life sciences corridor that runs from Headington to the Oxford Science Park. BMW Plant Oxford in Cowley produces the Mini hatchback and employs over 4,000 people, sustaining a supply chain of engineering and logistics firms across OX1 to OX4. Oxford University Press, one of the world\u2019s oldest publishing houses, remains a major employer in the City Centre. The tech sector is smaller than Cambridge\u2019s but growing, with clusters in Jericho and around the Oxford Science Park. This mix of higher education, biotech, automotive, and publishing creates a fragmented but sophisticated demand for accounting services.",
