      body: "Take an Aberdeen engineering firm in Bridge of Don buying \u00a3187,000 of subsea inspection equipment for a North Sea contract, where the whole cost has been dropped into the main pool for writing down allowances at eighteen percent without testing what was available in the year of spend. New and unused main rate plant can instead attract the Annual Investment Allowance, whose \u00a31,000,000 limit comfortably covers a purchase of this size. On those facts the whole \u00a3187,000 is deducted in the year of spend, and at the main corporation tax rate of 25 per cent that is \u00a346,750 of corporation tax relieved in that period rather than dripping out of the pool over many years. The difference is timing rather than total relief, but for an offshore contractor timing is cashflow.",
