    whyHere: "Kingston's economy runs on a distinctive mix of university spin outs, tech startups around the Town Centre and Surbiton, and established professional services firms in New Malden and Norbiton. We meet clients where they work: some prefer in person at a booked room near the Town Centre, others use our remote first setup. Either way, we bring careful technical judgement to corporation tax, VAT, and payroll for businesses that range from a three person digital agency to a thirty employee healthcare practice.",
    businessScene: "Kingston University anchors the local economy, producing a steady flow of graduates who launch tech and digital ventures in the Town Centre and Surbiton. Bentalls and John Lewis remain retail anchors, though the high street now competes with online. Kingston Hospital is a major employer in healthcare, while Unilever maintains a regional presence that draws professional services firms into the area. The result is a fragmented but resilient business scene: sole trader consultants sit alongside twenty person software companies and established partnerships in law and accountancy. New Malden has a notable concentration of Korean owned businesses, many operating as limited companies with cross border tax needs. Norbiton hosts a growing cluster of creative and marketing agencies. The local economy is not dominated by a single industry, which suits a generalist firm like ours.",
