      headline: "Worked example: \u00a312,774 net R&D benefit and stranded input VAT",
      body: "Take a Surbiton digital agency with eight staff, three years into custom platform development, with no R&D claim made. Assessed properly, the qualifying activity usually sits in the algorithm work and in structured user testing rather than in the visible front end. Suppose that activity costs \u00a385,160 across the build. At the merged scheme rate of 20 per cent the expenditure credit is \u00a317,032, and because the credit is itself taxable the net benefit at the 25 per cent main rate is \u00a312,774. A second and separate issue is common in the same business: a partial exemption calculation applied to a mix of standard and zero rated supplies, when zero rated sales are taxable and carry full recovery. Getting that wrong leaves input VAT stranded on costs that should recover in full. A quarterly review keeps both points from recurring.",
