      headline: "Worked example: \u00a319,200 net R&D credit on \u00a3128,000 of spend",
      body: "Take a Livingston microelectronics firm in Deans Industrial Estate that has built a new sensor assembly line, spending \u00a386,000 on software development and \u00a342,000 on prototype materials over two years, a total of \u00a3128,000 of qualifying expenditure. Under the merged R&D expenditure credit scheme the credit runs at 20 per cent of qualifying spend, so the gross credit is \u00a325,600. The credit is itself taxable, so at the UK main corporation tax rate of 25 per cent the net benefit is \u00a319,200. Aligning the VAT return cycle with the manufacturing cycle is a separate housekeeping point that removes duplicated administrative work.",
