    businessScene: "Hatfield sits at the intersection of the A1(M) and A414, with a business scene anchored by the University of Hertfordshire (over 30,000 students and a substantial research base), Ocado Group's global headquarters in the Town Centre, and EE's Hatfield campus (part of BT Group). Nearby Tesco's Welwyn headquarters adds a retail and consumer goods dimension. The aerospace legacy, from de Havilland to the current airfield and museum, still influences local engineering and maintenance firms. The postcode areas AL9 and AL10 cover a mix of science park units, retail parks and converted Victorian premises in Old Hatfield. Public sector contracts, university procurement and Ocado's supply chain create steady demand for accountants who understand grant accounting, R&D credits and VAT on cross border goods.",
