    whyHere: "Tonbridge businesses range from professional services firms in the Town Centre to tech startups in Higham Wood and construction companies in Hildenborough. We offer remote-first support with in-person meetings on request, covering corporation tax, VAT, payroll, and R&D credits. Local directors get technical rigour without the London premium. We understand the nuances of a town where Tonbridge School and Tonbridge and Malling Council are major employers, and where contractors and small business owners need clear, practical advice.",
    businessScene: "Tonbridge's economy is shaped by its historic role as a market town and its modern commuter links to London. The Town Centre hosts a mix of independent retailers, professional services firms (including Cluttons' regional office), and hospitality businesses. Education is a dominant force: Tonbridge School, a major local employer, drives demand for support services and residential construction. Tech firms cluster in Higham Wood and the Castle area, often founded by former London commuters. Construction remains steady, with firms serving both residential developments and commercial fit-outs in Hildenborough. EDF Energy maintains a regional presence, adding a layer of engineering and energy-sector work. The local economy is resilient but not high-growth, so businesses here value cost control and tax efficiency over aggressive expansion.",
