      headline: "Worked example: \u00a331,180 of CIS deductions and \u00a3168,200 of qualifying plant",
      body: "Take an eight person construction firm at Hildenborough where CIS deductions on subcontracted groundwork were never picked up, and which has just built a depot outside Tonbridge. Three years of subcontractor payment records will show what was deducted at source and never set against the company\u2019s own liabilities. Suppose those records show \u00a3155,900 of subcontract labour payments taxed at the 20% CIS rate, which is \u00a331,180 deducted at source. The depot then needs a separate exercise: the electrical systems, heating and security installations are plant within a building rather than structure, and suppose the fit-out invoices support \u00a3168,200 of qualifying expenditure. Only the CIS element is cash; the allowances reduce taxable profit, worth \u00a342,050 at the 25% main rate.",
