      business_type: "15-employee logistics operator",
      headline: "Worked example: \u00a325,800 of recoverable input tax on freight handling",
      body: "Take a Dover freight forwarder of around 15 staff with a yard on the Aycliffe estate, where every cross-border movement has been treated as outside the scope and the ancillary services swept along with it. Port handling and storage fees linked to EU imports are a different supply from the transport itself, and the input tax on them is not automatically blocked. Working through two years of invoice flow and attributing each cost to taxable, exempt or residual use, suppose \u00a3154,800 of VAT inclusive handling and storage fees fall to taxable use. The VAT fraction of one sixth of that gives \u00a325,800 of recoverable input tax. The point is structural rather than one-off: once the attribution is set out, each later return follows the same method instead of guessing.",
