      body: "Take a Worthing insurance broker of around 15 staff in the town centre, writing policies for UK and European clients, charging VAT across the board and paying output tax without reclaiming input VAT on the EU related costs. Intermediary services supplied to business customers outside the UK are generally outside the scope of UK VAT, and outside the scope does not mean input tax is blocked. On a four year review, suppose \u00a3166,300 of standard rated costs are attributable to those supplies, which at the 20 per cent standard rate is \u00a333,260 of input tax recoverable and never recovered. Once the invoicing distinguishes the two client groups at source, each later quarter follows the same attribution instead of being reconstructed. The four year cap is the practical limit, so the delay itself costs money.",
