    sectorEmphasis: "The local economy in Bognor Regis means our service emphasis shifts according to sector. A tourism business in Felpham or Pagham, for example, often needs help with VAT partial exemption and seasonal payroll planning. The hospitality sector here generates irregular income patterns, so we focus on cash flow forecasting and corporation tax timing. Manufacturing clients, including those supplying Rolls Royce at Goodwood, come to us for capital allowances on plant and machinery and R&D tax credits on process automation. Public sector contractors working with Arun District Council or St Richard's Hospital require careful IR35 assessment and limited company accounting. Retail businesses in the Town Centre frequently ask about VAT thresholds and business rates relief. We also see growing demand from healthcare professionals, including locum GPs and private physiotherapists, who need specialist tax planning around pension annual allowances and practice structures. Each sector brings distinct compliance and advisory priorities, and we tailor our approach accordingly.",
    keyEmployers: ["Butlin's Bognor Regis", "Rolls-Royce (Goodwood nearby)", "St Richard's Hospital (Chichester)", "Arun District Council", "Body Shop (legacy ops)"],
    localCaseStudy: {
      business_type: "15-employee tourism operator",
      headline: "Worked example: \u00a337,460 of input VAT on a mixed-use park renovation",
      body: "Take a Bognor Regis holiday park operator at Pagham, part way through a significant property renovation, told the VAT on the works is irrecoverable because some of the accommodation is exempt. That conclusion is often reached too early. Holiday accommodation is generally standard-rated, and where units are mixed, the intended use of each one, evidenced by the build contract and the booking pattern, drives the attribution. Suppose the build contract shows \u00a3187,300 of works attributable to the taxable accommodation. At the 20% standard rate that is \u00a337,460 of recoverable input tax on these facts. A seasonal trade should also align its return periods to the income pattern, which moves the repayment closer to the winter months when the cash is tightest.",
    },
    localFaqs: [
      { question: "Do you have an office in Bognor Regis?", answer: "There is no Holloway Davies office in Bognor Regis and we do not pretend otherwise. Meetings happen where you are, in the Town Centre, Aldwick, Felpham or Pagham, and for a seasonal tourism business that usually means October rather than the middle of August. Day to day the work runs by secure portal and video call." },
      { question: "My tourism business has seasonal staff. Can you handle fluctuating payroll?", answer: "Yes. We regularly manage payroll for hospitality and tourism businesses in Bognor Regis that hire heavily from April to September. We set up flexible RTI submissions and handle holiday pay accruals, auto enrolment, and year end returns without fixed monthly fees." },
      { question: "I supply goods to Rolls Royce at Goodwood. Do you handle R&D tax credits?", answer: "Yes, where the project meets the test. For a Goodwood supplier the qualifying work is typically in process development, jig and tooling design and automation, and it counts only where the project sought an advance in science or technology and the route was genuinely uncertain; machining to a customer's drawing does not qualify, however fine the tolerance. We prepare the technical narrative and the cost breakdown. Claims run under the merged RDEC scheme for accounting periods beginning on or after 1 April 2024." },
      { question: "What records do you need to take over my limited company accounts in Bognor Regis?", answer: "Your last three years of accounts, your recent VAT returns and the company authentication code. We then make the changes at HMRC and Companies House and send professional clearance to your previous firm. There is no penalty from HMRC or Companies House for switching mid year, and we schedule the changeover around your next filing date." },
    ],
