      headline: "Worked example: \u00a339,820 R&D expenditure credit on propeller design software",
      body: "Take a Torquay marine engineering firm in workshops near the harbour, developing bespoke software to model propeller hydrodynamics, with the activity real but the documentation thin. Documentation is the usual constraint rather than eligibility. Rebuilding the record from timesheets, subcontractor invoices and consumables issued to the project puts a costed boundary around the development, and suppose on those facts it supports \u00a3199,100 of qualifying expenditure, worth \u00a339,820 at the 20% merged scheme credit rate before the corporation tax charge on the credit. Workshop equipment bought in the same period sits in a different regime: first year allowances are a deduction against profit, not a cash credit, and the two reliefs are claimed separately even when they arise from the same project.",
