    businessScene: "Yeovil has long been defined by helicopter manufacturing, first through Westland Helicopters and now through Leonardo Helicopters UK, which employs thousands of engineers, technicians, and support staff. This industrial base supports a broad supply chain of precision engineering and fabrication firms, many of them family-run limited companies. The public sector is also significant: Yeovil District Hospital and South Somerset District Council are major employers, creating demand for contractors and professional services. The Town Centre and Hendford Hill host a mix of independent retailers, hospitality businesses, and healthcare practices. Smaller industrial estates in Yeovil Marsh and Preston Plucknett house specialist manufacturers and logistics operators. The local economy is relatively self-contained, meaning businesses here often serve a local or regional customer base rather than a national one, which shapes their tax and compliance needs.",
