      headline: "Worked example: \u00a340,940 R&D credit on an automated drilling rig",
      body: "Take a Yeovil subcontractor with fifteen staff machining parts for helicopter manufacture, two years into developing an automated drilling rig to hold tolerances on titanium components, with no R&D claim ever made. The qualifying expenditure here is materials consumed in the trials, subcontracted testing and the design manager\u2019s time apportioned to the project. Suppose that comes to \u00a3204,700 costed that way, giving a credit of \u00a340,940 at the 20% merged scheme rate before the corporation tax charge on the credit. A partly exempt business faces a separate calculation: overheads used for both taxable and exempt supplies are recoverable only in proportion, and the method has to reflect the actual split rather than a rule of thumb.",
