    sectorEmphasis: "Our service emphasis in Bridgwater is shaped directly by the local sector mix. For businesses in the Hinkley Point C supply chain, we organise corporation tax planning around long-term project cycles, structure R&D claims for engineering innovations, and handle complex CIS and VAT partial exemption rules. A fabrication firm in Sydenham might come to us for capital allowances on a new welding facility; a logistics operator on the A38 often needs help with payroll for irregular shift patterns and fuel duty recovery. Agriculture remains a significant part of the portfolio: a Wembdon dairy farmer might prioritise succession planning and agricultural property relief, while a cider producer needs VAT advice on zero-rating and flat-rate schemes. The public sector presence, through the Council and College, means we also advise on service company structures and consultancy arrangements for former employees. The mix is unusual for a town of 41,000: heavy engineering, high-value manufacturing, logistics, and primary production all within a few miles. That breadth forces us to be generalists who can specialise quickly, which is exactly how a well-run accounting firm operates.",
