      headline: "Worked example: \u00a341,460 R&D credit on welding automation",
      body: "Take a Sydenham steel fabricator with fifteen staff winning subcontracts on turbine hall works at Hinkley Point C, which has spent heavily on a robotic welding line and jig design but assumes only inventors qualify for R&D relief. They do not. Custom automation and the iterative testing needed to make it hold tolerance are qualifying activity. Suppose the record supports \u00a3207,300 of qualifying expenditure. Costed under the merged R&D expenditure credit scheme at 20%, the credit is \u00a341,460 before the corporation tax charge on it. Construction Industry Scheme returns raise a separate risk on phased contracts: monthly returns are due whether or not a payment falls in the period, and each late return carries its own penalty.",
