      headline: "Worked example: \u00a360,300 corporation tax saving from capital allowances",
      body: "Take a Cranford logistics company with eight vans and a 12,000 sq ft warehouse, where earlier returns claimed capital allowances on vehicles only. The work involved in a case like this is a sweep of the fixed asset register for expenditure missed elsewhere: racking, mezzanine flooring and a pallet wrapping machine installed over the previous two years. Allocating that spend to the right pools and claiming the Annual Investment Allowance in full converts it into a deduction in the year of purchase. Suppose the sweep identifies \u00a3241,200 of qualifying expenditure: at the 25 per cent main rate of corporation tax the relief is worth \u00a360,300. The same register then supports a forward plan for a later fleet expansion.",
