    businessScene: "Barnet is a large, economically diverse London borough. The Royal Free London NHS Trust and Barnet Council are major local employers, alongside Middlesex University in nearby Hendon and Saracens Rugby at the StoneX Stadium in High Barnet. Retail is concentrated around Brent Cross Shopping Centre and the high streets of High Barnet and Whetstone. The borough also has a strong independent healthcare sector, with numerous GP practices, dental surgeries and care homes. Real estate activity is steady, driven by family-held portfolios and small developers working on infill projects. The local economy is resilient rather than flashy, with most businesses focused on service delivery rather than high-growth scaling. This creates a stable base for a generalist practice that can handle everything from payroll for a 10-person dental surgery to corporation tax for a property company.",
