      headline: "Worked example: \u00a345,180 of VAT recoverable on a heritage vessel refit",
      body: "Take an eight-person Thames tour boat operator running services from the Cutty Sark pier and refitting a heritage vessel. VAT on passenger transport is the point of difficulty: carriage in a vessel carrying ten or more passengers is zero rated, while a guided commentary trip can be a different supply, so the ticket mix drives everything. Both are taxable supplies, so the input tax on the refit follows the use of the vessel rather than the rate charged. Suppose the refit invoices carry \u00a3225,900 of standard rated work used wholly for those trips: the recoverable VAT is \u00a345,180 at 20 per cent. A gift shop and caf\u00e9 on board bring exempt or mixed use into the picture and add a partial exemption calculation on top.",
